---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="KL Divergence — Made Visual"
  description="An interactive visual guide to KL divergence: what it is, how it's computed, and where it shows up in LLMs and PPO training."
  image="/blogs/KL-divergence-og.png"
>

<div id="read-progress"></div>

<div class="blog-shell">
  <div class="nav-column">
    <nav id="section-nav" aria-label="Section navigation">
      <div class="section-index-label mono">Index</div>
      <ul class="section-index" id="sectionIndex"></ul>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <article class="blog-post">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="section" id="s0" data-label="Intro">
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="hero-tag mono">10 min read · ML Fundamentals</div>
      <h1>KL Divergence<br><em>made visual</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub"><em>Kullback–Leibler divergence</em> — no scary math. Just two distributions,<br>and how far apart they are.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Section 1 — Distribution -->
  <section class="section" id="s1" data-label="Distributions">
    <div class="section-label mono">01 — The Big Idea</div>
    <h2>What even is a distribution?</h2>
    <p>Before KL Loss, let's get comfortable with distributions. A <strong>probability distribution</strong> tells you how likely each outcome is. Think of it as a "belief" about what will happen.</p>
    <p>Below are two distributions — <strong>P</strong> (the true one) and <strong>Q</strong> (our guess). Drag the sliders and watch them shift.</p>

    <div class="canvas-wrap">
      <canvas id="distCanvas" height="155"></canvas>
      <div class="controls">
        <span class="ctrl-label mono">P peak position</span>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="100" value="35" id="pPeak" step="1">
        <span class="ctrl-val mono" id="pPeakVal">35%</span>
      </div>
      <div class="controls">
        <span class="ctrl-label mono">Q peak position</span>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="100" value="65" id="qPeak" step="1">
        <span class="ctrl-val mono" id="qPeakVal">65%</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      <p>When P and Q overlap perfectly, they're identical. When they drift apart — that gap is exactly what KL divergence measures.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2 — Formula -->
  <section class="section" id="s2" data-label="The Formula">
    <div class="section-label mono">02 — The Formula</div>
    <h2>What KL divergence actually measures</h2>
    <p><strong>Kullback–Leibler divergence</strong> (KL) answers: <strong>"How much extra information do I waste if I use Q to describe a world that's actually P?"</strong></p>

    <div class="formula-box">
      <div class="formula mono">KL(P ∥ Q) = Σ P(x) · log( P(x) / Q(x) )</div>
      <div class="formula-sub">Sum over all outcomes x. P is truth, Q is our approximation.</div>
    </div>

    <p>Three things to notice:</p>
    <div class="props-list">
      <div class="prop-item">
        <span class="prop-num mono">1.</span>
        <span>It's <strong>not symmetric</strong> — KL(P∥Q) ≠ KL(Q∥P). Direction matters.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prop-item">
        <span class="prop-num mono">2.</span>
        <span>It's always <strong>≥ 0</strong>. Zero means the distributions are identical.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prop-item">
        <span class="prop-num mono">3.</span>
        <span>The <strong>log ratio</strong> captures surprise — when Q says something is rare but P says it's common, that's expensive.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3 — Live Calculation -->
  <section class="section" id="s3" data-label="Live Calc">
    <div class="section-label mono">03 — Live Calculation</div>
    <h2>Let's compute it ourselves</h2>
    <p>Hit <strong>Random</strong> to shuffle two full distributions over Rain, Sunny, and Cloudy. P is truth; Q is the forecast.</p>

    <div class="calc-panel">
      <div class="calc-panel-header">
        <div class="calc-panel-heading">
          <span class="calc-panel-title mono">Total KL(P ∥ Q)</span>
          <span class="calc-panel-sub">P · log(P/Q) summed over all three outcomes</span>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-kl-pill mono">
          <span class="calc-kl-val" id="klResult">—</span>
          <span class="calc-kl-unit">nats</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <button type="button" class="calc-random-btn" id="calcRandom">Random distributions</button>

      <div class="calc-body">
        <div class="calc-stacks" id="calcStacks"></div>
        <div class="calc-penalty-col">
          <div class="calc-penalty-list" id="klBreakdown"></div>
          <div class="calc-equation mono" id="klEquation"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4 — Which direction? -->
  <section class="section" id="s4" data-label="Which Direction">
    <div class="section-label mono">04 — Which Direction?</div>
    <h2>What if the loss is KL(P ∥ Q) or KL(Q ∥ P)?</h2>
    <p>Same two distributions — but the direction flips who weights the sum and which ratio you take. In training, <strong>P is frozen</strong> (truth / parent). Only <strong>Q, the student</strong>, gets updated.</p>

    <div class="dir-setup">
      <div class="dir-model dir-model-frozen">
        <span class="dir-badge dir-badge-frozen mono">Frozen</span>
        <span class="dir-model-inline"><strong>P — truth / parent</strong> · Fixed reference · never moves during training</span>
      </div>
      <span class="dir-arrow mono">same P · two different losses on Q ↓</span>
      <div class="dir-model dir-model-train">
        <span class="dir-badge dir-badge-train mono">Trained</span>
        <span class="dir-model-inline"><strong>Q — student model</strong> · Starts identical · diverges by loss function</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="dir-viz">
      <div class="dir-viz-cols">
        <span class="dir-viz-col-label mono">KL(P ∥ Q) loss</span>
        <span class="dir-viz-col-label mono">KL(Q ∥ P) loss</span>
      </div>
      <canvas id="dirAnimCanvas" height="128"></canvas>
      <div class="dir-viz-footer">
        <span class="dir-viz-step mono" id="dirAnimStep">Step 0 / 48</span>
        <button type="button" class="dir-viz-replay" id="dirAnimReplay">Replay training</button>
      </div>
      <p class="dir-viz-legend mono" id="dirAnimExplain">Purple = P (frozen) · Green = Q (student updating each step)</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dir-compare">
      <div class="dir-card dir-card-forward">
        <h4>Forward · KL(P ∥ Q)</h4>
        <div class="dir-formula mono">Σ P(x) · log( P(x) / Q(x) )</div>
        <ul class="dir-points">
          <li><strong>P weights</strong> the sum · ratio <strong>P/Q</strong></li>
          <li>Q spreads to <strong>cover all modes</strong> — blurry but inclusive</li>
          <li>Watch left panel: Q widens across both peaks</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="dir-card dir-card-reverse">
        <h4>Reverse · KL(Q ∥ P)</h4>
        <div class="dir-formula mono">Σ Q(x) · log( Q(x) / P(x) )</div>
        <ul class="dir-points">
          <li><strong>Q weights</strong> the sum · ratio <strong>Q/P</strong></li>
          <li>Q <strong>locks onto one mode</strong> — sharp, mode-seeking</li>
          <li>Watch right panel: Q snaps to a single peak</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Section 5 — The question each KL asks -->
  <section class="section" id="s5" data-label="The Question">
    <div class="section-label mono">05 — The Question Each KL Asks</div>
    <h2>Two different questions — RLHF picks one</h2>
    <p>Forward and reverse KL are not just swapped formulas. Each one asks a <strong>different question</strong> about frozen P and trained Q. In RLHF, we care far more about the reverse one.</p>

    <div class="kl-question-compare">
      <div class="kl-question-card kl-question-forward">
        <h4>Forward KL(P ∥ Q)</h4>
        <p class="kl-question-main">"If <strong>P is truth</strong>, where is Q <strong>missing mass</strong> that P cares about?"</p>
        <p class="kl-question-sub">Expectation under <strong>P</strong> · punishes Q for being too low where P is high · pushes Q to <strong>cover every mode</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="kl-question-card kl-question-reverse">
        <h4>Reverse KL(Q ∥ P)</h4>
        <p class="kl-question-main">"Where <strong>Q actually puts mass</strong>, is it saying things <strong>P would not</strong>?"</p>
        <p class="kl-question-sub">Expectation under <strong>Q</strong> · punishes Q for being high where P is low · keeps the student <strong>on a leash</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kl-rlhf-box">
      <div class="kl-rlhf-header">
        <span class="kl-rlhf-badge mono">RLHF · PPO</span>
        <h3>Why reverse KL is what we use</h3>
      </div>
      <ul class="kl-rlhf-points">
        <li><strong>P stays frozen</strong> — the SFT parent we trust. <strong>Q is trained</strong> with reward signals on its own outputs.</li>
        <li>We only sample from <strong>Q</strong> during RL — reverse KL weights exactly those tokens, asking whether the student is drifting off-policy.</li>
        <li>Forward KL would force Q to spread across all of P's modes — useful in VI, but <strong>too blurry</strong> for coherent language.</li>
        <li>Reverse KL is the right guardrail: improve from reward, but stay close to the parent. Hence <span class="mono">reward − β · KL(Q ∥ P)</span>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <!-- Section 6 — Token by Token -->
  <section class="section" id="s6" data-label="Token by Token">
    <div class="section-label mono">06 — Token by Token</div>
    <h2>Reverse KL on every token the student writes</h2>
    <p class="token-lead">Ask <em>"What is the capital of France?"</em> — the student replies below. Click any word (or use <span class="mono">← →</span>) to see how far <strong>Q</strong> drifted from frozen parent <strong>P</strong> at that step.</p>

    <div class="token-stage">
      <div class="token-pick">
        <div class="token-pick-bar">
          <span class="token-pick-label mono">Student reply · click a token</span>
          <div class="sentence-box" id="tokenSentence"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="token-stepper">
          <button type="button" class="token-nav-btn" id="tokenPrev" disabled aria-label="Previous token">
            <span class="token-nav-arrow">←</span>
          </button>
          <div class="token-dots" id="tokenDots" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <span class="token-step-indicator mono" id="tokenStepIndicator">—</span>
          <button type="button" class="token-nav-btn" id="tokenNext" disabled aria-label="Next token">
            <span class="token-nav-arrow">→</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="token-detail" id="tokenDetail">
        <div class="token-detail-head">
          <div class="token-detail-focus">
            <span class="token-inspector-label mono">Token</span>
            <span class="token-badge mono" id="tokenTitle">—</span>
          </div>
          <div class="token-kl-pill mono">
            <span class="token-kl-label">KL(Q∥P)</span>
            <span class="token-kl-val" id="tokenKL">—</span>
            <span class="token-kl-unit">nats</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="token-insight" id="tokenInsight"></p>

        <div class="token-detail-grid">
          <div class="token-zone token-zone-ctx">
            <div class="token-zone-title mono">Where we are</div>
            <div class="token-context-panel" id="tokenContext"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="token-zone token-zone-bars">
            <div class="token-zone-title mono">What each model would say next</div>
            <div class="token-compare token-compare-stack">
              <div class="token-model-block token-model-p">
                <div class="token-model-label">
                  <span class="dot" style="background:#7F77DD"></span> P · parent (frozen)
                </div>
                <div class="token-bar-list" id="parentBars"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="token-model-block token-model-q">
                <div class="token-model-label">
                  <span class="dot" style="background:#1D9E75"></span> Q · student (trained)
                </div>
                <div class="token-bar-list" id="studentBars"></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="token-zone token-zone-calc">
            <div class="token-zone-title mono">Penalty on the word Q picked</div>
            <div class="token-calc-highlight" id="tokenCalcHighlight"></div>
            <div class="token-calc-total mono" id="tokenCalcTotal"></div>
            <p class="token-calc-note">In PPO, we sum KL(Q∥P) across every token the student actually writes.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 7 — Recap -->
  <section class="section" id="s7" data-label="Recap">
    <div class="section-label mono">Recap</div>
    <h2>The 30-second summary</h2>
    <div class="recap-list">
      <div class="recap-item">
        <span><strong>KL divergence</strong> measures how different distribution Q is from distribution P.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="recap-item">
        <span><strong>Forward KL</strong> asks where Q misses P's mass. <strong>Reverse KL</strong> asks where Q oversteps P — the question RLHF actually needs.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="recap-item">
        <span><strong>RLHF / PPO</strong> uses reverse KL(Q∥P): reward improves Q, but <span class="mono">−β·KL(Q∥P)</span> keeps it near frozen parent P.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="recap-item">
        <span><strong>Reverse KL</strong> is used in self-distillation for sharper, mode-seeking behavior.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  </article>
</div>

</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── Full-screen scroll snap ── */
  :global(html) {
    scroll-snap-type: y mandatory;
    scroll-padding-top: 50px;
  }
  :global(body > .page-shell > footer) {
    display: none;
  }

  /* ── Progress bar ── */
  #read-progress {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    height: 2px;
    width: 0%;
    background: #7F77DD;
    z-index: 9999;
    transition: width 0.1s linear;
  }

  /* ── Shell: nav column + content column (no overlap) ── */
  .blog-shell {
    --content-width: 56rem;
    --nav-width: 7.5rem;
    --shell-gap: 2rem;
    --shell-width: min(calc(var(--content-width) + var(--nav-width) + var(--shell-gap)), calc(100vw - 3rem));
    width: var(--shell-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: var(--nav-width) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--shell-gap);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .nav-column {
    width: var(--nav-width);
    min-height: 1px;
    position: relative;
  }

  /* ── Section index (left; active centered, others faded) ── */
  #section-nav {
    position: fixed;
    top: 50%;
    left: 1.75rem;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    z-index: 100;
    width: max-content;
    max-width: 11rem;
    overflow: visible;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .section-index-label {
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-3);
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
    padding-left: 0.1rem;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .section-index {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    pointer-events: auto;
  }
  :global(.section-index-item) {
    display: block;
    width: max-content;
    max-width: 11rem;
    text-align: left;
    border: none;
    background: none;
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    padding: 7px 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--text-3);
    opacity: 0.5;
    white-space: nowrap;
    transition: opacity 0.35s ease, color 0.35s ease;
  }
  :global(.section-index-item:hover) {
    opacity: 0.72;
  }
  :global(.section-index-item.active) {
    opacity: 1;
    color: #534AB7;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"] .section-index-item.active) {
    color: #9B93F0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .blog-shell {
      --content-width: min(56rem, calc(100vw - 3rem));
      --shell-width: var(--content-width);
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
    }
    .nav-column,
    #section-nav { display: none; }
  }

  /* ── Layout ── */
  .blog-post {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /* ── Hero ── */
  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 0; }
  .hero-tag {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-3);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .hero h1 em {
    font-family: "Lora", serif;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #7F77DD;
  }
  .hero-sub {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* ── Sections (one viewport below nav; content centered, no inner scroll) ── */
  .section {
    --section-h: calc(100vh - 50px);
    --section-h: calc(100dvh - 50px);
    height: var(--section-h);
    min-height: var(--section-h);
    max-height: var(--section-h);
    overflow: hidden;
    scroll-snap-align: start;
    scroll-snap-stop: always;
    scroll-margin-top: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    justify-content: safe center;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  .section > :first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .section h2 { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }
  .section p { margin-bottom: 0.55rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .section .callout { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
  .section .canvas-wrap { margin: 0.65rem 0; padding: 0.75rem; }
  .section .formula-box { margin: 0.65rem 0; padding: 1rem; }
  .section .props-list { margin: 0.45rem 0; gap: 0.45rem; }
  .section .ppo-box { margin: 0.65rem 0; padding: 1rem; }
  .section .controls { margin: 0.35rem 0; }
  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-3);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  p {
    font-size: 0.925rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-2);
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }
  p strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }
  p em { font-family: "Lora", serif; font-style: italic; }

  .divider {
    display: none;
  }

  /* ── Callout ── */
  .callout {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-left: 3px solid #7F77DD;
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }
  .callout p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .callout-tight {
    padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
    margin: 0.45rem 0 !important;
  }
  .callout-tight p { font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  /* ── Live calc panel ── */
  .calc-panel {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
  }
  .calc-panel-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.65rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .calc-panel-heading {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }
  .calc-panel-title {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }
  .calc-panel-sub {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }
  .calc-kl-pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 5px 12px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: #EEEDFE;
    border: 1px solid #AFA9EC;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .calc-kl-pill {
    background: #1d1c35;
    border-color: #3d3870;
  }
  .calc-kl-val {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #534AB7;
  }
  .calc-kl-unit {
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .calc-kl-val { color: #9B93F0; }

  .calc-random-btn {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 7px;
    border: 1px solid #AFA9EC;
    background: #EEEDFE;
    color: #534AB7;
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
  }
  .calc-random-btn:hover {
    background: #e0ddf8;
    border-color: #7F77DD;
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .calc-random-btn {
    background: #1d1c35;
    border-color: #3d3870;
    color: #9B93F0;
  }
  :global([data-theme="dark"]) .calc-random-btn:hover {
    background: #252347;
    border-color: #7F77DD;
  }

  .calc-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.05fr);
    gap: 0.85rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .calc-penalty-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  .calc-stacks {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }
  :global(.calc-stack-row) {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }
  :global(.calc-stack-label) {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  :global(.calc-stack-wrap) {
    display: flex;
